
COMPARATIVE GENOME ANALYSIS USING BLASTn

Organisms:
1. Bacillus subtilis strain 168
2. Bacillus licheniformis strain DSM 13

Method:
Local nucleotide sequence alignment using BLASTn.

RESULTS:

Total BLAST alignments: 782
Average percentage identity: 86.55%
Length-weighted identity: 83.10%
Highest percentage identity: 100%
Longest alignment: 19,915 bp

Genome Coverage:
B. subtilis 168: 23.28%
B. licheniformis DSM 13: 22.81%

Query bases covered: 981530 bp
Subject bases covered: 963161 bp

CONCLUSION:

BLASTn analysis identified regions of nucleotide
similarity between the two Bacillus genomes.
The aligned regions showed variable sequence identity,
indicating differences in sequence conservation.
Approximately 23% of each genome was covered by
the reported local alignments.
